1. What this covers.
   This licence covers the Civic-Chain Grant & Budget Auditor engine, its
   skill package, its rulesets, and all accompanying files in this repository
   published on or after the cut-over commit recorded in CHANGELOG.md. Versions
   published before that commit were offered under the MIT Licence and remain
   available to anyone who already holds them under those MIT terms. This
   licence does not revoke any MIT grant already made.

2. Grant.
   While the licensee holds an active Civic-Chain subscription, Civic-Chain
   grants a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to install and run the
   software on the licensee's own systems, against the licensee's own data, for
   the licensee's own auditing purposes.

3. Source-available, not open source.
   The source is published so that the licensee may inspect it. Inspection does
   not grant any right to redistribute, resell, sublicense, publish, or create
   derivative works for distribution. "Open source" is not an accurate
   description of this licence and must not be used for it.

4. No redistribution or resale.
   The licensee may not distribute, resell, rent, lease, or make the software
   available to any third party, whether modified or unmodified.

5. No warranty.
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

6. Limitation of liability.
   IN NO EVENT SHALL CIVIC-CHAIN BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
